            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>Taking the train between Alexandria and Fredericksburg offers a short, convenient trip. It's often comparable to or faster than driving during rush hour, and allows you to relax, use Wi-Fi, stretch your legs, and enjoy views of the Potomac River, Quantico Marine Base, and Virginia's historic countryside. Compared to road travel, the train avoids I-95 traffic, notorious for congestion in this corridor, and delivers you straight into Fredericksburg's charming historic downtown without needing a car. </p>
