            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography </h2>
            <p>
                The Alexandria-to-Fredericksburg train route runs along the historic RF&P Railroad corridor (Richmond, Fredericksburg & Potomac), traveling southwest from the Potomac River through Northern Virginia's rolling countryside. Passengers get views of the Potomac River, Quantico Marine Corps Base, Prince William Forest Park, and the historic Rappahannock River valley, making the journey more than just transit; it's a relaxed and picturesque experience through one of America's most historically significant regions.
                The route passes through key locations, including Quantico and Woodbridge, before reaching Fredericksburg. Along the way, travelers can enjoy natural scenery, including the Potomac River shoreline, military installations, suburban Virginia development, and glimpses of historic Civil War battlefields.
            </p>
