            <h2>Tips to Save Money on This Route</h2>
            <p>Managing the cost of train travel from Alexandria to Fredericksburg is easier with some planning and smart strategies. With multiple service options available, travelers can optimize their spending based on travel frequency and priorities. </p>
            <h3>Plan for Better Price Options </h3>
            <ul>
                <li>VRE Monthly Passes: Daily commuters should purchase VRE monthly passes for significant savings over single-ride fares. The cross-honor agreement with Amtrak provides additional value.</li>
                <li>Advance Booking (Amtrak): Purchasing Amtrak tickets days or weeks ahead often secures the lowest fares, especially for Northeast Regional Coach. Fares can start as low as $6 with early purchase.</li>
                <li>Compare Services: For occasional travel, compare VRE and Amtrak fares; sometimes Amtrak early-bird fares rival VRE pricing with added comfort.</li>
                <li>Amtrak Guest Rewards: Sign up for Amtrak's loyalty program to earn points toward future travel.</li>
                <li>Student &amp; Senior Discounts: Amtrak offers discounts that can significantly reduce fares on the Northeast Regional.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Travel During Off-Peak Hours</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Midday Amtrak Trains:</b> Often less crowded, with fares sometimes lower than morning and evening peak services.</li>
